      "never_emit_reason": "BROKEN UPSTREAM, and the breakage is ansible-core-version dependent. The four perm.yml includes pass `item.value.<full|change|read|deny> | split(',') | trim`: `split` returns a LIST and Jinja's `trim` is a STRING filter. On ansible-core >= 2.16 (jinja2 3.x) that raises 'expected string or bytes-like object' and the play dies part-way through, leaving shares created but unpermissioned; on older cores it can coerce and hand win_acl one mangled principal. The trailing `| default([])` rescues nothing — it substitutes only for an UNDEFINED left-hand side, and it sits AFTER the filter that throws. Note also that the defaults on full/change/read/deny exist only in the win_share task; the perm includes reference those keys BARE, so omitting one is a second, independent failure. Plant shares with a post_clone script, or use `permissions` against an explicit path.",
